User wants to view a time series chart on the Fact Promotion detail page (localhost:3000/plan/fact/*) to visualize the variation of base volume and promo volume against dates.

REQUIREMENTS:

1. CHART LOCATION:
   - The time series chart should be placed after the Summary table (Summary Card section) on the Fact Promotion detail page
   - The chart should be displayed in a dedicated section with proper styling consistent with the page design

2. CHART DATA:
   - X-axis: Dates (from the promotion's date range)
   - Y-axis: Volume values
   - Display two data series:
     * Base Volume (base_volume_snapshot from Fact_Promotions)
     * Promo Volume (promo_volume_estimate from Fact_Promotions)
   - Both series should be clearly distinguished using different colors/styles

3. AGGREGATION LEVEL TOGGLE:
   - Provide ability to view chart at two aggregation levels:
     a) Aggregated Level (All Products): 
        - Sum base_volume_snapshot and promo_volume_estimate across all products for each date
        - This is the default view
     b) Individual Products:
        - Allow user to select a specific product (via dropdown/selector)
        - Show base volume and promo volume for the selected product only
        - Display product name (sku_name) when individual product is selected

4. TIME AGGREGATION TOGGLE:
   - Provide ability to toggle between three time aggregation levels:
     a) Daily: Show data point for each date (default)
     b) Weekly: Aggregate volumes by week (sum volumes for all dates within each week)
        - Week should be defined as Monday-Sunday or Sunday-Saturday
        - Display week range (e.g., "Jan 1-7, 2024") on x-axis
     c) Monthly: Aggregate volumes by month (sum volumes for all dates within each month)
        - Display month name and year (e.g., "January 2024") on x-axis

5. DATA PROCESSING:
   - For aggregated (all products) view:
     * Group records by date/time period
     * Sum base_volume_snapshot across all products for each time period
     * Sum promo_volume_estimate across all products for each time period
   - For individual product view:
     * Filter records by selected product_id
     * Group by date/time period
     * Sum base_volume_snapshot for the selected product across all customer/region/channel combinations for each time period
     * Sum promo_volume_estimate for the selected product across all customer/region/channel combinations for each time period
   - Handle null values appropriately (treat as 0 for aggregation)

6. UI COMPONENTS:
   - Product Selection Control:
     * Radio buttons or dropdown to select "All Products" or "Individual Product"
     * When "Individual Product" is selected, show a dropdown listing all unique products (sku_name) from the promotion records
     * Default to "All Products"
   - Time Aggregation Control:
     * Radio buttons or toggle buttons for "Daily", "Weekly", "Monthly"
     * Default to "Daily"
     * Show selected aggregation level clearly

7. CHART LIBRARY:
   - Use Recharts library (already available in package.json)
   - Chart type: Line chart or Area chart
   - Features:
     * Interactive tooltip showing exact values for both series on hover
     * Legend to distinguish between Base Volume and Promo Volume
     * Responsive design that works on different screen sizes
     * Proper date formatting on x-axis
     * Grid lines for better readability

8. DATA SOURCE:
   - Chart data should be derived from the existing API response at /api/promotions/fact/:id
   - Process the records array client-side to create chart data points
   - No additional API endpoint required initially (can be optimized later if needed)

9. STYLING:
   - Match the existing design system (dark mode support, consistent colors)
   - Chart container should have:
     * White/dark background matching page theme
     * Rounded corners and border consistent with other cards
     * Proper padding and spacing
   - Chart colors should be:
     * Distinct colors for Base Volume and Promo Volume (e.g., blue for base, green for promo)
     * Accessible color contrast

10. PERFORMANCE:
    - Chart should handle large datasets efficiently
    - Use useMemo for data processing to avoid unnecessary recalculations
    - Only recalculate chart data when:
      * Records data changes
      * Product selection changes
      * Time aggregation level changes

11. ERROR HANDLING:
    - If no data available, show appropriate message
    - Handle edge cases (empty date ranges, no volumes, etc.)
    - Show loading state if data is being fetched
